You can use a "simple" logger to record an event. It will record one word at a time, without printing a log file.
Example:
public class SimpleLogging {
    private static SimpleLogging logger = new SimpleLogging();
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        logger.print("test");
    }
    public static void printTest() {
        logger.info("Testing");
    }
}

You can't record a word of text, you can only record an event.

